# Git guesses binary by sniffing for NUL bytes, and a small PDF can contain
# none at all — the generated résumé has zero NULs and eighty LFs, so git
# classified it as text. With core.autocrlf=true a fresh clone would then
# rewrite those LFs as CRLFs, shifting every byte offset in the file. PDF
# cross-reference tables are absolute byte offsets, so the file arrives broken.
#
# Nothing below is a formatting preference. It is what keeps binaries intact
# across a clone.

* text=auto

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
